# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 permu.cc stddev (the list and matrix path of stddev, stddevp and variance, column by column) summed x^2 in one pass and subtracted s*mean^2, which cancels in floats: at Digits 12 variance([1.1,1.1,1.1]) = -7.1e-15 (right 0, a variance is never negative), variance([0.3,0.3,0.3]) = 4.4e-16, stddevp([0.7,0.7,0.7]) = 1.03e-07 (right 0), and at higher Digits a stored float list gave a negative variance and an imaginary deviation (N62 Home: variance of approx([1/10,1/10,1/10]) -1e-62, stddevp 1e-31*i). Now a column holding a float (has_num_coeff) takes two passes about its first value x0: m = mean(x-x0), sum((x-x0-m)^2), so equal values give an exact 0 and the sum is a sum of squares; an exact column keeps the one-pass formula (exact anyway). The frequency forms (stddevmean in misc.cc) are not changed.
